<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ioannina</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yanina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ioannina is the largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, on the shore of Lake Pamvotis. A leading city of the medieval Despotate of Epirus, it surrendered to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1430. Around 1800 it was the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-pasha-of-yanina">Ali Pasha of Tepelena</a>, who ruled much of mainland Greece from its citadel. It became part of Greece in 1913.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ioannina.jpg" alt="Ioannina" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SilentResident (compilation, sources to attribute see above; if any of the sources used in the Montage are removed fr... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ioannina_Montage_L.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
